      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Not really problem, since WMR users can go to virtual desktop world and add things to virtual desktop browser.\nAnd Vive/Oculus have also own virtual desktop so they can open browser there and type missing parts.\n\nNo need pop it up inside VRChat. The VR Headset software have already own solutions for it.\nSteamVR has also desktop view option.\n\nWhen done, you can go back to VRChat.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-11-16T03:28:07.476Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I think the ability of being able to access the canny.io page for VRChat from within the game would be cool. Because this means that instead of playing the game, and coming across a bug, or thinking of a feature that could be added, then having to end your play session, then open up a web browser, which ends up with you forgetting what you were going to post on there. I think it would be more efficient to be able to access it from within the game (now for desktop only users this is much easier with alt-tab) but this would be much better for players who use VR, especially for people who live stream this game, and find a bug or think up a feature but can't just end the steam or tab out of the game.",
